WEBVTT

00:02.304 --> 00:05.431
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.539 --> 00:09.169
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.278 --> 00:12.679
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.781 --> 00:15.476
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:16.017 --> 00:19.146
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.254 --> 00:22.450
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.623 --> 00:24.021
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.124 --> 00:25.615
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.993 --> 00:30.861
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:36.202 --> 00:41.197
Mom, Dad, I decided I want a big party
this year with all my friends.

00:41.609 --> 00:43.905
And maybe a band? Is that cool?

00:44.243 --> 00:47.338
- Yeah, sure. Yeah, why not? Sure.
- Yeah, sure. Yeah, why not? Sure.

00:47.447 --> 00:49.541
Oh, thanks, guys, you're the best.

00:50.215 --> 00:52.480
What's she talking about?
A party for what?

00:52.585 --> 00:55.645
I don't know. She have her period
or something? Is she getting married?

00:55.755 --> 00:57.221
No, if she was getting married,

00:57.323 --> 00:58.882
we probably would have
seen a guy around, right?

00:58.992 --> 00:59.959
Sound reasoning.

01:00.059 --> 01:04.894
- You guys. It's Meg's birthday next week.
- Oh, my God. It is.

01:04.997 --> 01:06.862
Peter, we got to put together a party.

01:06.966 --> 01:09.161
Oh, man, I hate kids' birthday parties.

01:09.268 --> 01:10.928
This is gonna be worse
than that time I was stuck

01:11.036 --> 01:13.129
behind Robert Loggia at the airport.

01:13.238 --> 01:16.072
- May I have your name please?
- Robert Loggia.

01:16.176 --> 01:17.141
Can you spell that for me?

01:17.241 --> 01:22.508
Certainly. That's Robert Loggia.
R as in Robert Loggia.

01:22.815 --> 01:26.115
O as in "Oh, my God, it's Robert Loggia."

01:26.484 --> 01:29.817
B as in "By God, that's Robert Loggia."

01:30.188 --> 01:33.646
E as in "Everybody loves Robert Loggia."

01:34.193 --> 01:36.989
R as in Robert Loggia.

01:37.394 --> 01:40.762
T as in " Tim, look over there,
it's Robert Loggia."

01:41.265 --> 01:42.391
Space.

01:42.632 --> 01:45.466
L as in "Look, it's Robert Loggia."

01:45.570 --> 01:46.537
(SIGHS)

01:51.141 --> 01:52.699
- Here you are, Brian.
- What's this?

01:52.809 --> 01:55.573
It's an invitation to Meg's party.
I'm the party planner.

01:55.680 --> 01:58.274
You have to RSVP.
You could do it right now if you want.

01:58.383 --> 02:02.682
- All right, fine. I'll come to Meg's party.
- No, you have to call the RSVP line.

02:02.918 --> 02:05.251
- You got to be kidding me.
- I'm waiting.

02:06.023 --> 02:08.184
(SIGHING) Ring, ring.

02:09.025 --> 02:09.992
Aren't you gonna pick it up?

02:10.092 --> 02:12.856
No, I'm not gonna pick it up
on the first few rings. I'm busy.

02:12.962 --> 02:14.624
Maybe I'm in the other room.

02:14.731 --> 02:20.999
Ring, ring. Ring, ring. Ring, ring.

02:22.338 --> 02:24.272
- Ring. Come on.
- Hello.

02:24.373 --> 02:25.361
- Stewie?
- No.

02:25.474 --> 02:29.068
This is Stewie's housekeeper,
Mrs. Pennyapple. I'll see if he's in. Stewie.

02:29.177 --> 02:31.077
- Stewie.
- Yes, Mrs. Pennyapple?

02:31.179 --> 02:32.841
- You've got a telephone call.
- Who is it?

02:32.948 --> 02:34.813
- He didn't say.
- Well, find out, would you?

02:34.917 --> 02:36.315
- Who is this?
- It's Brian.

02:36.418 --> 02:38.011
- It's Brian.
- Oh, Brian.

02:38.120 --> 02:41.021
Probably RSVPing about Megan's party.
Hello, Brian.

02:41.123 --> 02:42.589
- Hi, Stewie.
- What can I do for you?

02:42.690 --> 02:43.816
I'm coming to Meg's party.

02:43.925 --> 02:46.450
Oh, splendid, just give
your information to Mrs. Pennyapple.

02:46.561 --> 02:49.996
Hello, it's Mrs. Pennyapple again.
Shall I put you down for two, Brendan?

02:50.097 --> 02:51.088
- Brian.
- Ryan.

02:51.200 --> 02:52.188
- Brian.
- Mitchell.

02:52.300 --> 02:53.562
- What?
- Goodbye.

02:55.236 --> 02:57.101
Hey, Lois, I'm ordering a birthday cake

02:57.205 --> 03:00.139
and the guy wants to know how old
Meg is. I didn't know what to tell him.

03:00.241 --> 03:02.105
- You're asking me?
- Yeah, how old is Meg?

03:02.209 --> 03:03.233
Well, I don't know.

03:03.343 --> 03:06.210
Well, my God, Lois. I thought you were
the one keeping track of that.

03:06.313 --> 03:08.143
No, no, I have no idea.

03:08.247 --> 03:11.614
Don't you remember me faking
my way through her last birthday?

03:11.852 --> 03:15.549
<i>You are... going on...</i>

03:15.655 --> 03:18.784
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

03:18.926 --> 03:22.759
Should we just ask her how old she is?

03:23.196 --> 03:25.358
That'd be kind of awkward, huh?

03:25.699 --> 03:28.724
Hey, maybe we should just cut off her leg
and count the rings.

03:28.835 --> 03:33.569
- Yeah, or maybe try carbon-dating.
- I don't know what that is.

03:33.674 --> 03:35.970
You know,
we're gonna have to talk to her

03:36.074 --> 03:39.306
and kind of steer the conversation
in a way that gets her to spill it.

03:39.412 --> 03:40.401
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

03:40.513 --> 03:41.479
Come in.

03:41.581 --> 03:43.549
- Hi, sweetie.
- Hey, Meg.

03:43.649 --> 03:46.777
So, Meg, your birthday's coming up, huh?

03:46.886 --> 03:50.321
You excited about turning...

03:52.924 --> 03:56.381
Meg, I got 16 candles
for your birthday cake.

03:56.928 --> 03:59.419
- How does that sound?
- That's not right.

03:59.531 --> 04:03.365
So less, more,

04:03.468 --> 04:06.631
too many, not enough?

04:06.738 --> 04:10.298
You stupid son of a bitch,
you didn't even know how old I am.

04:10.407 --> 04:13.968
Meg, that kind of language is
not appropriate for a girl your age.

04:14.245 --> 04:16.076
Or is it?

04:16.447 --> 04:18.642
I'm gonna be 17, you jerks.

04:20.152 --> 04:21.641
She's the jerk.

04:25.789 --> 04:27.278
All right, come on in, everybody.

04:27.390 --> 04:28.358
Have a seat anywhere.

04:28.459 --> 04:30.722
Meg's gonna open her presents
in a little bit.

04:30.827 --> 04:34.058
Oh, Francis, I'm glad you could make it.

04:34.164 --> 04:37.429
- Here, this is for Megan.
- What is it?

04:37.534 --> 04:40.435
It's a cookie from lunch period
at the home.

04:40.537 --> 04:44.064
- Well, I'm sure she'll love this.
- I want to see her eat it.

04:44.274 --> 04:46.243
So the man asks the bartender
to recommend a good drink,

04:46.343 --> 04:49.675
and the bartender says a grasshopper,
so the guy orders a grasshopper.

04:49.779 --> 04:50.745
Then he's walking home

04:50.846 --> 04:53.315
and along the way he notices
a grasshopper on the ground.

04:53.415 --> 04:56.748
So he says to the grasshopper, " Hey, you
know there's a drink named after you?"

04:56.852 --> 05:00.288
The grasshopper says,
"You mean, there's a drink named Irving?"

05:03.959 --> 05:06.428
So, which one of you wants
to lose your virginity?

05:06.528 --> 05:07.961
Mom, this party sucks.

05:08.063 --> 05:12.261
I mean, balloons? Pin the Tail
on the Donkey? I'm not five years old.

05:12.367 --> 05:15.392
Meg, your father worked very hard
to put this party together.

05:15.503 --> 05:17.699
And he says he's got
a big surprise for you.

05:17.806 --> 05:21.707
Hey, kids, I'm Pee-Pants,
the inebriated hobo clown.

05:21.809 --> 05:26.179
I'm an adorable tramp who wears found
clothing and eats out of your garbage can.

05:26.280 --> 05:29.215
A clown? Dad, I'm 17.

05:29.317 --> 05:32.115
Meg, guess what Pee-Pants
got you for your birthday?

05:32.220 --> 05:34.620
- A scarf.
- I don't want a scarf, Dad.

05:34.755 --> 05:37.918
Well, then, how about a dozen scarves?

05:38.059 --> 05:39.457
(SINGING)

05:41.828 --> 05:42.988
(COUGHS)

05:44.232 --> 05:47.667
Peter, I don't think you're actually
supposed to swallow those.

05:48.435 --> 05:49.993
(COUGHING)

05:54.040 --> 05:55.029
Here you go, Meg.

05:55.141 --> 05:57.303
- I don't want them.
- Take them.

05:57.644 --> 05:59.736
Hey, are my long johns tied
to the end of those?

05:59.845 --> 06:01.279
- No.
- Oh, God.

06:01.481 --> 06:02.879
(RETCHING)

06:07.019 --> 06:09.783
(GROANING)

06:12.225 --> 06:15.352
- Mom, can I just open my presents now?
- All right, Meg.

06:15.462 --> 06:17.396
Thank you. What the...

06:17.497 --> 06:19.293
Hey, let's see what else we got here.

06:19.398 --> 06:22.798
<i>The first season of Sister, Sister on DVD.</i>

06:22.901 --> 06:24.027
BOY: You're welcome.

06:24.136 --> 06:27.002
Stewie, what are you doing?
You can't open Meg's gifts.

06:27.106 --> 06:30.131
Hey. These are mine. You hear me? Mine.

06:30.442 --> 06:34.275
Oh, God. Not the "mine" phase.
I've been dreading this day.

06:34.379 --> 06:35.903
I'm entitled to these things, Lois,

06:36.013 --> 06:39.848
especially after I got shafted
by that Asian Santa at the mall.

06:39.951 --> 06:41.475
What do you want for Christmas?

06:41.586 --> 06:44.350
I was thinking maybe
one of those old-timey...

06:44.455 --> 06:46.615
Too late. Take too long. Sad Christmas.

06:46.723 --> 06:47.986
- What you want?
- Fire truck.

06:48.092 --> 06:49.058
- What color?
- Red.

06:49.159 --> 06:50.148
Next.

06:51.795 --> 06:53.525
Peter, have you been drinking?

06:53.631 --> 06:57.397
- Well, a little. It is a party.
- Take off that stupid costume.

06:57.502 --> 06:58.661
You look like a damn fool.

06:58.769 --> 07:02.637
Oh, Dad, you won't say that
when you see my grand unicycle finale.

07:02.739 --> 07:04.139
Everyone, I'll be right back.

07:04.242 --> 07:08.109
In the meantime, I leave you
with the musical stylings of Chris Griffin.

07:10.580 --> 07:16.712
<i>I don't know what we're afraid of</i>

07:17.154 --> 07:23.092
<i>Nothing would change if we made love</i>

07:23.327 --> 07:28.661
<i>So I'll be your friend</i>

07:30.067 --> 07:35.469
<i>And I'll be your lover</i>

07:36.105 --> 07:37.072
(SIGHS)

07:37.540 --> 07:40.236
All right,
this is gonna blow you guys away.

07:40.576 --> 07:41.837
(SCREAMING)

07:42.445 --> 07:43.810
- Grandpa!
- Oh, my God.

07:43.913 --> 07:45.846
- Is he breathing?
- Somebody call an ambulance.

07:45.947 --> 07:48.881
Lois, maybe you better
call two ambulances.

07:53.655 --> 07:54.713
How is he, Doctor?

07:54.823 --> 07:57.916
Mrs. Griffin, his internal injuries
were much too severe.

07:58.026 --> 08:00.392
I'd estimate he'll be dead within the hour.

08:00.495 --> 08:03.862
Dad, I'm so sorry I broke all your ribs
and busted your spleen

08:03.965 --> 08:05.329
and punctured your lung.

08:05.432 --> 08:07.899
I don't know if you can hear me right now,

08:08.135 --> 08:11.103
but I hope you know I love you, Dad.

08:11.605 --> 08:17.668
Peter, come closer.
There's something I need to say to you.

08:17.777 --> 08:19.541
I'm here, Dad. What is it?

08:19.947 --> 08:24.178
Peter, you're a fat, stinking drunk.

08:24.283 --> 08:25.807
(CARDIOGRAPH FLATLINING)

08:25.918 --> 08:30.617
Oh, my God, he's dead. He can't be dead.
There's got to be something I can do.

08:30.990 --> 08:33.357
Maybe I'll bury him in the pet cemetery.

08:34.226 --> 08:35.626
(BOTH SCREAMING)

08:37.163 --> 08:39.097
Okay, I'll bury him in a regular cemetery.

08:44.467 --> 08:46.196
I can't believe Grandpa's dead.

08:46.303 --> 08:51.240
Well, he did kind of treat us like crap,
but, yes, it is a tragedy.

08:51.341 --> 08:52.740
It is a tragedy.

08:52.843 --> 08:55.107
- Excuse us.
- Yeah, we'll be right back.

08:56.112 --> 08:57.579
(INAUDIBLE)

09:05.688 --> 09:07.747
- We're all gonna miss him.
- Tragic.

09:07.856 --> 09:09.223
You know what the worst part is?

09:09.326 --> 09:12.157
All I wanted was for my dad to tell me
he loved me.

09:12.260 --> 09:14.957
But instead he called me
"a fat, stinking drunk."

09:15.064 --> 09:16.462
Those were his last words.

09:16.564 --> 09:21.399
Well, I hate to side with your father, Peter,
but you do kind of drink a lot.

09:21.502 --> 09:24.801
And you know,
sometimes it affects the people you love.

09:25.139 --> 09:27.106
Oh, my God. Lois, you're right.

09:27.341 --> 09:31.039
Booze made me fall down all those stairs.
Booze killed my father.

09:31.179 --> 09:35.879
Well, from this day forward,
I, Peter Griffin, will never drink again.

09:40.087 --> 09:42.147
- Peter, what're you doing?
- Crack.

09:42.257 --> 09:45.020
- What the fuck?
- Hey, at least I'm not drinking, Brian.

09:45.125 --> 09:48.561
Yeah, this isn't exactly a good substitute.
Where'd you get crack?

09:48.662 --> 09:49.924
- From Black's.
- What?

09:50.030 --> 09:52.862
Yeah, right behind Black's hardware store,
there's a white guy selling it.

09:52.965 --> 09:54.957
Look, doing crack is not
the way to stop drinking.

09:55.068 --> 09:59.061
You need to get to the heart of why you
feel the need to drink in the first place.

09:59.172 --> 10:02.572
Look, here. This is the number
of a hypnotherapist I want you to see.

10:02.675 --> 10:04.337
- All right, Brian.
- Good.

10:09.582 --> 10:12.380
Hey, Peter, just thought I'd check on you.
Oh, my God!

10:12.485 --> 10:15.283
Government came and took my baby.

10:18.291 --> 10:22.126
This is mine and this is mine
and that's mine and this is mine.

10:22.694 --> 10:23.821
Oh, what's this?

10:23.930 --> 10:27.365
"Hot Monogamy,
the board game for failing marriages."

10:28.635 --> 10:31.101
"Dare Card. Have her do a striptease

10:31.202 --> 10:33.898
"and see how long it takes you
to get a bonner."

10:34.607 --> 10:35.630
What's a bonner?

10:35.740 --> 10:38.470
Stewie, what are you doing
with my jewelry box?

10:38.577 --> 10:41.238
- Now, you give that back to Mommy.
- No, go to hell.

10:41.346 --> 10:45.577
Stewie, I have had just about enough
of this new selfish attitude of yours.

10:45.683 --> 10:47.583
Now give that back to Mommy.

10:47.686 --> 10:50.382
Very well, then.
If I can't have it, nobody can.

10:50.522 --> 10:54.788
- That is enough.
- You struck me.

10:54.893 --> 11:00.524
Oh, my God. Stewie, honey, I am so sorry.
Are you okay, sweetie?

11:02.232 --> 11:03.597
(CRYING)

11:04.501 --> 11:08.562
Oh, honey, I'm sorry,
Mommy would never hurt you.

11:08.672 --> 11:10.139
Let me give you a hug.

11:10.240 --> 11:11.968
(CONTINUES CRYING)

11:13.710 --> 11:17.169
I haven't been this scared
since Mother Teresa OD'd in my car.

11:17.281 --> 11:18.770
She is messed up, man.

11:18.881 --> 11:21.372
Shut up. Just shut up.
Let me fucking think.

11:21.884 --> 11:23.647
- Push her out.
- We can't leave her alone.

11:23.753 --> 11:25.186
Push the bitch out.

11:29.458 --> 11:33.087
Okay, for starters,
why don't you just lay back and relax?

11:33.196 --> 11:37.564
Loosen up them trousers.
Now, feel the air between them toes.

11:38.233 --> 11:41.032
Feel a gentle wind blowing
the hair on them legs.

11:41.471 --> 11:43.938
Breezing up on through
the rest of your body,

11:44.039 --> 11:46.872
through your private areas,
through your anus.

11:47.610 --> 11:50.772
Now let's go back in your mind
to your childhood,

11:50.879 --> 11:52.937
to some of your deepest memories,

11:53.348 --> 11:55.339
maybe some that aren't so happy.

11:56.017 --> 11:58.315
You know, the anus has
the second-highest density

11:58.419 --> 12:00.284
of nerve endings in the body.

12:01.323 --> 12:03.018
You remembering anything?

12:03.158 --> 12:05.022
Like maybe being the best at jump rope

12:05.126 --> 12:08.721
and not being allowed to win the ribbon
just because you was a boy?

12:08.829 --> 12:12.559
Or being told everything you made
in pottery class was inappropriate?

12:12.665 --> 12:14.634
Yeah, I'm getting something.

12:15.936 --> 12:18.995
- Happy Father's Day, Dad.
- I'm not your father.

12:19.540 --> 12:23.908
Oh, my God.
Francis Griffin wasn't my real father.

12:24.143 --> 12:26.203
I wonder what else I've repressed?

12:26.312 --> 12:29.213
Oh, my God. I could've had a V8.

12:32.451 --> 12:34.852
It was horrible, Rupert.
It was like a nightmare.

12:34.954 --> 12:38.548
Lois came at me like a wild animal.
I had no way to defend myself.

12:39.325 --> 12:41.919
Mother, I'm sorry
I went against your wishes.

12:42.128 --> 12:43.595
(GROWLING)

12:44.663 --> 12:47.690
I'm sorry I misbehaved, Mother.
I'm sorry I misbehaved.

12:47.801 --> 12:49.462
It won't happen again.

12:50.235 --> 12:52.203
I love you, Mommy dearest.

12:52.304 --> 12:53.271
(GROANS)

12:53.505 --> 12:54.904
(GROWLING)

12:57.275 --> 12:58.572
It was awful, Rupert.

12:58.676 --> 13:04.309
I felt terrified and brutalized
and humiliated and alive.

13:04.949 --> 13:07.851
My God, I haven't felt that alive in years.

13:08.287 --> 13:12.313
Rupert, you know, I think perhaps
I may be one of those people

13:12.624 --> 13:14.558
who gets a jolly out of being hit.

13:14.660 --> 13:19.187
Stewie, there you are.
Mommy is so sorry she hit you.

13:19.530 --> 13:22.090
I promise I will never
lay a hand on you again.

13:22.200 --> 13:25.100
Well, let's not make any rash decisions.
I mean, I did provoke you.

13:25.202 --> 13:28.730
Come on, Lois, hit me.
Beat the crap out of me, step on my cubes.

13:31.308 --> 13:32.935
(DOORBELL RINGING)

13:34.978 --> 13:38.414
Oh, hi, Peter.
Are you here to bring back the TV set?

13:38.515 --> 13:41.609
No, I sold it for crack. But listen, Mom,
I got to ask you something.

13:41.718 --> 13:43.309
Who's my real father?

13:44.354 --> 13:48.381
I knew this day would come.
All right, Peter, here it is.

13:48.492 --> 13:51.722
About 40 years ago,
I was vacationing in Ireland

13:51.827 --> 13:54.956
and I met a young rogue
named Mickey McFinnegan.

13:55.065 --> 13:58.295
Peter, Mickey is your real father.

13:58.534 --> 14:01.163
Oh, my God. I got to find him.

14:03.505 --> 14:04.837
To Ireland.

14:10.546 --> 14:12.309
Sweetheart, when will you be back?

14:12.414 --> 14:13.402
I don't know, Lois,

14:13.515 --> 14:16.177
all I know is somewhere
in the great land of Ireland

14:16.284 --> 14:18.879
is a big, fat bastard who looks like me.

14:19.120 --> 14:23.056
Call me as soon as you can, Peter.
And I really hope you find your real father.

14:23.158 --> 14:27.425
- We're gonna miss you, Dad.
- Come back soon, Daddy. I love you.

14:27.662 --> 14:29.959
That'll do, pig, that'll do.

14:33.334 --> 14:35.858
There she is, Rupert. Oh, if I can
just get her to hit me one more time,

14:35.969 --> 14:38.130
it'll give me the rush I've been looking for.

14:38.238 --> 14:39.297
(EX CLAIMS)

14:39.407 --> 14:40.396
(LAUGHS)

14:40.508 --> 14:42.134
Oh, what's next? What's next?
What's next?

14:42.242 --> 14:43.733
Oh, God. I've been so bloody naughty.

14:43.844 --> 14:46.039
Oh, I need to be taught a lesson
and you're the one to do it.

14:46.146 --> 14:47.205
(EX CLAIMS)

14:47.981 --> 14:52.246
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

14:52.519 --> 14:55.181
Yeah, all that stuff,
let's make that happen.

14:56.455 --> 14:59.983
- Oh, hi, sweetie, you want some juice?
- Oh, that would be lovely.

15:01.929 --> 15:03.726
- Oh, Stewie.
- Yeah.

15:04.063 --> 15:07.966
- Look at the mess you made.
- Oh, I've made a terrible mess, haven't I?

15:08.067 --> 15:10.558
Yes, I've made you take time
out of your day to clean up my mess

15:10.670 --> 15:12.296
and I should be punished for it. Go.

15:12.405 --> 15:15.499
Well, I guess it's not that big a deal.
Accidents happen.

15:15.608 --> 15:18.872
Oh, I don't know. Don't you think you
should spank me or slice my nostril?

15:18.978 --> 15:22.310
- It's all right, Stewie, now go play.
- Oh, all right.

15:24.649 --> 15:28.813
Look, I've drawn heavyweight pugilist
David Tua on the wall. Punish me.

15:28.920 --> 15:32.754
Sweetie, you really gotta...
Looks like David Tua.

15:32.857 --> 15:35.917
You've really got to stop misbehaving.
You're getting on Mommy's nerves.

15:36.027 --> 15:37.494
Well, you know
what will ease your stress?

15:37.596 --> 15:39.587
Slap me across the face like a bitch.

15:39.699 --> 15:41.928
It's all right. I'll get some Windex.

15:42.133 --> 15:43.430
Come on. Discipline me.

15:43.535 --> 15:45.799
Make me wear panties,
rub dirt in my eye,

15:45.904 --> 15:49.863
violate me with a wine bottle. My God.
I really do have problems, don't I?

15:53.178 --> 15:55.907
<i>PILOT: Welcome to Ireland.
We'll be landing in five minutes.</i>

15:56.013 --> 15:57.480
This is quite a country, Brian.

15:57.581 --> 16:00.244
You know, Ireland has
more drunks per capita than people.

16:00.352 --> 16:01.545
Oh, that's a negative stereotype.

16:01.652 --> 16:04.916
I don't think the Irish drink
as much as people say they do.

16:15.465 --> 16:18.161
Excuse me, is this McSwiggen Village?

16:18.268 --> 16:20.862
Devil a man who'll say
a word against it, hmm?

16:21.003 --> 16:22.028
Is that a yes or a no?

16:22.138 --> 16:26.542
Aye, it is McSwiggen Village, where
the hills are green, the streams are clear

16:26.644 --> 16:30.044
and the sweaters are so thick,
even the boniest-fingered nun

16:30.146 --> 16:32.273
could poke you in the chest
and it wouldn't bother you none.

16:32.382 --> 16:36.045
Don't be so bold with your dark hair
and your proud ways.

16:36.152 --> 16:37.515
I can't feel a thing.

16:37.619 --> 16:38.917
Hey, what are those guys doing?

16:39.022 --> 16:41.047
Those are the McMurphy brothers.

16:41.156 --> 16:43.988
They've been circling that same spot
for 50 years,

16:44.091 --> 16:46.926
just daring each other to throw
the first punch.

16:47.029 --> 16:49.054
- Just you try it.
- Oh, I'll try it.

16:49.165 --> 16:51.098
- Just you try it.
- You'll feel it when I try it.

16:51.199 --> 16:53.928
- I'd like to see you have at it.
- Would you now?

17:00.842 --> 17:03.468
Hey, you heard of a man
named Mickey McFinnegan?

17:03.576 --> 17:05.705
Have I heard of him?
Of course I've heard of him.

17:05.814 --> 17:07.041
He's the town drunk.

17:07.148 --> 17:09.083
Town drunk? Oh, my God.

17:09.184 --> 17:11.777
You mean,
he's the disgrace of the whole town?

17:13.255 --> 17:15.313
You lads aren't from around here,
are you?

17:15.423 --> 17:18.483
Top of the morning, laddies.
Let me cut you an Irish rose.

17:18.592 --> 17:19.650
(FARTS)

17:21.795 --> 17:24.263
I don't know exactly where
the County Cork is,

17:24.364 --> 17:26.265
but I know where it should be.

17:29.503 --> 17:33.029
Around here the town drunk
is a person of great honor.

17:33.606 --> 17:37.702
- Excuse me, sir. My name is Peter.
- Pleased to meet you, lad. Name's Mickey.

17:37.811 --> 17:42.475
Listen, this may be hard for you to believe,
but you're my father.

17:42.682 --> 17:44.273
Oh, am I now?

17:44.383 --> 17:46.817
Yeah, I came all the way from America
to find you.

17:46.919 --> 17:50.946
I suppose it's money you're wanting.
I owe you some allowance and so forth.

17:53.960 --> 17:57.622
Oh, no, I don't want money, I just want
to get to know you and be friends.

17:57.730 --> 18:00.995
So I can finally have a real dad
who loves and respects me.

18:01.100 --> 18:04.159
You can't be me son,
you and me are nothing alike.

18:04.268 --> 18:05.760
Just ask me sheep, O'Brian.

18:05.872 --> 18:09.533
Whose leg do you have to hump
to get a pint of Guinness around here?

18:11.143 --> 18:13.611
Boy, it's amazing, isn't it?
You get two fathers,

18:13.712 --> 18:15.612
and neither one of them wants
anything to do with you.

18:15.714 --> 18:16.804
There's got to be some way

18:16.914 --> 18:19.781
I can make him see
that I'm worthy of being his son.

18:19.917 --> 18:24.013
About the only way I could ever impress
him is if I was a fat stinking drunk.

18:24.122 --> 18:27.717
<i>FRANCIS: Peter, you're a fat,
stinking drunk.</i>

18:27.825 --> 18:31.090
- What?
- You're a fat, stinking drunk.

18:31.195 --> 18:33.321
Yes, from what he's told us
that's right on the money.

18:33.431 --> 18:34.727
Challenge him, you must.

18:34.831 --> 18:36.593
And I'm Hayden Christensen.

18:36.733 --> 18:40.226
Wait a minute, Brian. That's it.
I'm a fat, stinking drunk

18:40.538 --> 18:44.667
because my father is a fat, stinking drunk.
And I got to prove it to him.

18:44.775 --> 18:46.766
I have gotta drink him
so far under the table,

18:46.877 --> 18:48.935
he'll have no choice but to respect me.

18:49.044 --> 18:50.535
Get me a beer, Brian.

18:50.647 --> 18:51.910
I am gonna prepare for this

18:52.015 --> 18:54.744
as thoroughly
as Ben Affleck prepares for a role.

18:55.985 --> 18:58.478
I got to be Henry Vlll in 20 minutes.

18:58.588 --> 19:01.614
Hello. Hello. Hello. Hello. Got it.

19:04.594 --> 19:08.495
Mickey McFinnegan,
I challenge you to a drinking contest.

19:08.664 --> 19:10.063
(ALL GASPING)

19:10.166 --> 19:13.101
And what makes you think you can hold
your own with the likes of me?

19:13.202 --> 19:15.601
Because I'm your son and I'm tough.

19:15.937 --> 19:18.338
<i>I made it halfway through
Failure to Launch.</i>

19:18.441 --> 19:22.604
I just never managed to get my life
together, isn't that hilarious?

19:24.046 --> 19:25.273
You're cute.

19:25.580 --> 19:26.639
Done.

19:28.249 --> 19:29.306
As we say in Ireland,

19:29.416 --> 19:34.081
let's drink until the alcohol in our system
destroys our livers and kills us.

19:37.092 --> 19:38.524
I got 20 on the fat one.

19:38.626 --> 19:41.186
- Which one's the fat one?
- Which one's the fat one?

19:41.295 --> 19:43.127
(BOTH LAUGHING)

20:28.240 --> 20:29.469
(SHUDDERING)

20:30.142 --> 20:32.200
- What happened?
- Peter, you won.

20:32.310 --> 20:35.802
My God. Nobody's ever beat me
at the game of drink.

20:35.915 --> 20:37.906
Now do you believe that you're my dad?

20:38.016 --> 20:41.247
Nobody but a McFinnegan could handle
that much of the creature.

20:41.353 --> 20:44.220
You're the broth of me own
stubby shillelagh, all right.

20:44.322 --> 20:45.721
Welcome to me family, Peter.

20:45.825 --> 20:48.291
Did you hear that, Brian?
I'm a McFinnegan now.

20:48.392 --> 20:50.122
I can forget all about Francis.

20:50.228 --> 20:52.423
You know, there's something
you should always remember, Peter.

20:52.531 --> 20:56.695
Francis may not have been your father,
but he raised you as if you were his own.

20:56.801 --> 20:59.565
And if that isn't love, I don't know what is.

20:59.671 --> 21:02.901
Wow. I guess you're right,
but there is one thing, Mickey.

21:03.007 --> 21:05.202
You knocked up my mom
and never called her again.

21:05.309 --> 21:08.244
- Yeah, so what?
- So what? So let's dance.

21:08.444 --> 21:10.709
<i>Oh, he doesn't smell like Irish Spring</i>

21:10.814 --> 21:12.339
<i>And he never taught me anything</i>

21:12.449 --> 21:15.907
<i>But still I slap my chest and sing
of my drunken Irish dad</i>

21:16.020 --> 21:17.954
<i>Oh, his face looks like a railroad map</i>

21:18.055 --> 21:19.647
<i>And he never shuts his freakin' trap</i>

21:19.757 --> 21:23.124
<i>But all the ladies catch the clap
from your drunken Irish dad</i>

21:23.226 --> 21:25.991
<i>Ask a Hennessy, Tennessy, Morrison,
Shaughnessy, Riordan and Rooney</i>

21:26.096 --> 21:27.083
<i>They'll tell you the same</i>

21:27.196 --> 21:28.993
<i>McNulty, Mulroney
and Cotter and Clooney</i>

21:29.098 --> 21:30.793
<i>All feel the same mixture
of pride and of shame</i>

21:30.900 --> 21:32.528
<i>Finnegan, Hannigan, Kelly and Flannigan</i>

21:32.635 --> 21:34.432
<i>Look to the ground
when their dad passes by</i>

21:34.537 --> 21:36.095
<i>Cafferty, Rafferty, Joyce and O'Lafferty</i>

21:36.205 --> 21:40.665
<i>Fight for his honor and then start to cry</i>

21:56.625 --> 21:58.525
<i>Oh, we Irish lads are all infirm</i>

21:58.628 --> 22:00.322
<i>And our moods infect us like a germ</i>

22:00.429 --> 22:04.229
<i>'Cause we're all the spawn
of a pickled sperm</i>

22:04.333 --> 22:05.891
And we don't tan well, either.

22:06.000 --> 22:08.093
<i>From a drunken Irish dad</i>

22:08.094 --> 23:09.094
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru